TEXT 64 16 Left 3 ;#281 NPN switching-time test fixture
TEXT 64 80 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XgSKLsWAWGs
TEXT 64 128 Left 2 ;A pulsed base drive turns the DUT on and off; drive, base, and collector traces expose delay and storage.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 !.tran 0 5u 0 100p
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 !.meas tran IC_ON AVG Ic(Qdut) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 !.meas tran IB_ON AVG Ib(Qdut) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 !.meas tran VCESAT AVG V(CH1_COLLECTOR) FROM 2u TO 2.4u
TEXT 64 928 Left 2 !.meas tran OVERDRIVE PARAM IC_ON/IB_ON
TEXT 820 768 Left 2 !.meas tran TD TRIG V(CH2_DRIVE)=2 RISE=1 TARG Ic(Qdut)=2.2554m RISE=1
TEXT 820 808 Left 2 !.meas tran TR TRIG Ic(Qdut)=2.2554m RISE=1 TARG Ic(Qdut)=20.299m RISE=1
TEXT 820 848 Left 2 !.meas tran TS TRIG V(CH2_DRIVE)=2 FALL=1 TARG Ic(Qdut)=20.299m FALL=1
TEXT 820 888 Left 2 !.meas tran TF TRIG Ic(Qdut)=20.299m FALL=1 TARG Ic(Qdut)=2.2554m FALL=1
TEXT 820 928 Left 2 !.meas tran TON PARAM TD+TR
TEXT 820 968 Left 2 !.meas tran TOFF PARAM TS+TF
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;Alan's page 3 gives the 5 V supply, 220 ohm collector resistor, 1.2k base resistor, 50 ohm termination\nand the 2.2u and 1n decoupling. He does not name the device under test or his generator levels.
TEXT 64 1144 Left 2 ;The 10 and 90 percent trip points are 2.2554 mA and 20.299 mA, which are ten and ninety percent of the\n22.554 mA IC_ON reports. Change the device or the drive and those levels have to be recomputed.
